+### Time Format Compound
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h30m"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })      // "25h1m1s"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h30m"
+```
+
+Largest unit first, zero parts skipped, no separators. Smallest unit is seconds (leftover milliseconds are dropped, so `500` gives `"0s"`) and the largest is hours (`25h30m`, never days), so the output can be parsed by Go's `time.ParseDuration`. Ignored if `long` is set.
+
 ### Input Formats (Units)
 
 ```ts
